:: Dramatis Personae Data [script]
/*
	Character key -> { display, target }. "target" that looks like a URL
	renders as an external link (new tab, via SugarCube's own
	external-link detection); anything else is treated as a passage name
	for a local bio passage. Add new characters here.
*/
setup.characters = {
	"Marx": { display: "Karl Marx", target: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_Marx" },
	"Fukuyama": { display: "Francis Fukuyama", target: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Fukuyama" }
};

:: Dramatis Personae Widget [widget]
/% <<character "Key">> looks "Key" up in setup.characters and links its
   display name to a local bio passage or an external page, whichever is
   configured. Falls back to the raw key as plain text if not found. %/
<<widget "character">>\
<<if setup.characters.hasOwnProperty($args[0])>>\
<<set _character to setup.characters[$args[0]]>>\
[[_character.display->_character.target]]\
<<else>>\
<<= $args[0]>>\
<</if>>\
<</widget>>
